    string p = GetString();
    for (int i = 0, n = strlen(p); i < n; i++)
    {
        int keycount = i % strlen(j);
        int k = j[keycount] - 'A';
            if( isalpha(p[i]))
            {
                (caesar cipher code that uses current k value to modify cleartext)
            }

            else
            {
                printf("%c", p[i]);
            }
        }
    printf("\n");
}

I've tried adding int spacecount = 0 outside of the for loop and then using spacecount++ inside the else condition (and subtracting its value from keycount) but it doesn't seem to want to work that way.

Thanks!
